Servers widget: panel and SSH key                                                                   
                                                                                                    
Remnawave panel address and API token. Stored in ~/.config/serpantinum/secrets/ (600). You can      
skip it.                                                                                            
                                                                                                    
┌─ Servers widget ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Remnawave panel URL  https://panel.example.com                                                   │
│   + format looks right                                                                           │
│ Remnawave API token  ***************_                                                            │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
┌─ SSH key for the widget only ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ + ed25519 key created: ~/.config/serpantinum/servers/id_serp  SHA256:Q3c.example                 │
│ On every server add exactly this line to ~serp/.ssh/authorized_keys:                             │
│ restrict,command="/usr/local/sbin/serp-run" ssh-ed25519                                          │
│ AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIExampleKeyOnlyFakeFakeFakeFake0000 serpantinum                          │
│ The key can only run allowed commands (allowlist), no shell, no forwarding:                      │
│ status - diag-disk - diag-load - diag-logs - diag-net - diag-ports - diag-security               │
│ act-restart-node - act-update-container - act-docker-prune - act-reboot                          │
│ Easier: after the install press "Connect server" in the widget.                                  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                                                                                    
